    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` test requires the create AUDIT log line to contain both `membershipNumber` and `membershipLevel` (matching the values returned by `GET /owners/{id}`).\n\nI updated `AuditOwnerCreated.java` (the OfficeFloor function that emits the create audit line):\n\n- Injected the `OwnerMapper` Spring bean (resolved by type, per the function-injection convention) so the audit line derives `membershipNumber` the same way the response DTO does \u2014 `mapper.membershipNumber(owner)` \u2192 e.g. `NSW-16E6609E-M26`.\n- Added `membershipNumber={}` to the log format and argument list, keeping all previously logged fields (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`) intact.\n\nResult:\n```\nINFO AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-10-05 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26\n```\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0.",
