    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally sound and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- `membershipNumber` is a *derived* field (formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`), not a stored property on `Owner` \u2014 there is no `owner.getMembershipNumber()`. The canonical derivation lives in `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber(owner)` (`OwnerMapper.java:101`), which is also what the DTO mapping uses (`@Mapping(... expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")`).\n- Reusing that mapper method instead of re-implementing the `%s-M%02d` format string in the audit logger keeps a single source of truth and avoids duplication \u2014 exactly the right call.\n- `membershipLevel` is a genuine stored field, so reading it via `owner.getMembershipLevel()` is correct; the mix (direct getter for stored, mapper for derived) is consistent with how the mapper already treats derived fields (`timezone`, `checkDigit`, etc.).\n- The function stays small and single-purpose; injecting `OwnerMapper` by type is the normal bean-injection pattern per the project conventions. All previously logged fields remain.\n\nNo changes needed.",
